.TH MOIRA-CLAUDE-STATUSLINE 1 "August 2026" "moira 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moira\-claude\-statusline \- Claude Code status-line command for Moira
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moira\-claude\-statusline
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B moira\-claude\-statusline
is the status\-line command Claude Code invokes after a response. It
reads the structured JSON payload from standard input, updates Moira's
minimal local quota cache (never the rendered /usage screen), and chains
the previously configured status\-line command when one exists, so the
original output is preserved.
.PP
The command is installed and removed only by Moira itself: the Settings
view records the original status line and restores it on removal.
.SH INPUT
A single JSON object on standard input as documented by Claude Code for
status\-line commands. Malformed or non\-object input is ignored without
error.
.SH OUTPUT
Nothing is printed by
.B moira\-claude\-statusline
itself; when a delegate status line is configured, its standard output
and standard error pass through unchanged.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moira/claude-rate-limits.json
Minimal sanitized cache of the structured rate-limit data (normally
.IR ~/.local/state/moira/claude-rate-limits.json ).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moira/claude-integration.json
Moira-owned integration metadata, including the preserved original
status-line command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns the delegate command's exit status when one is configured, and
0 otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moira (1),
.BR moira\-agent\-hook (1)
